\end{equation}
This relation was obtained for different values of the mass of the fiducial nonrotating NS models (different values of $\rm x$ in $R_{\rm x}$). Specifically, we employ $R_{1.2}$, $R_{1.4}$, $R_{1.6}$ and $R_{1.8}$. In each case, the maximum residual and the {\it adjusted} coefficient of determination $R^2$  was evaluated (see Table \ref{table:fRM} in Appendix \ref{Appendix.E}). Below, we present for each post-merger frequency the empirical relation that has the smallest error.

